From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] server: Watch many directories on PS5.

A PS5 title can hold about 256 open files, and every watched directory
kept one. Java's watch service opens each folder it watches for
overlapped I/O, reads its file information, binds it to a completion port
and keeps a ReadDirectoryChangesW pending on it. Project Zomboid watches
the 1704 folders of its media tree that way, and its title ran out of
files at about the 240th. Patch 0871 parks a directory past the first 64,
but opens it again for good the first time it is used, and patch 0993
keeps every fd with an async queued, which a pending change watch is.

- A directory parked past that threshold now shares patch 0993's budget
  for read-only files: once it is opened again it is live, the client
  gets its descriptor uncached, and the least recently used is parked
  again. A directory has no position to restore; the name must still lead
  to a directory with the same device and inode. With
  WINE_PS5_PARK_FILES=0 it stays open once used, as before.
- Patch 0884 lists a watched directory by its name, so the change watches
  queued on a directory it polls do not keep the descriptor.
- One timer lists every watch in turn, instead of one timer each: every
  25 ms it lists the watches that are due, least recently listed first,
  for at most 1 ms (WINE_PS5_POLL_BUDGET_US), and the others wait for the
  next tick. A watch is still listed at most every 25 ms, and less often
  when its listing takes long. On a PC, 1500 watches with a timer each
  took 31% of a core while nothing changed; under the budget they take
  about 4%, and a change is reported in about 200 ms.
- A listing that fails for want of a descriptor or of memory is dropped
  rather than compared, which reported every entry missing from it as
  removed.
- -DPS5_POLL_CHANGES builds the polling on a PC, in place of inotify, so
  the console's code can be tested there.

tests/test_wine_directory_watch.py watches 1500 folders as Java does and
checks that a created and a renamed file are reported, and nothing else.
Under a host Wine and a 512-descriptor limit, the server without this
patch, built with PS5_PARK_DIRECTORIES and PS5_PARK_FILES, fails it with
STATUS_TOO_MANY_OPENED_FILES at the 244th folder; with this patch and
PS5_POLL_CHANGES as well it passes.
